<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=2044" title="Layers in soil defined by physical, chemical, biological, or mineralogical properties which vary with depth.">soil horizons</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1080" title="Natural resources of unconsolidated fragmented rock, humus, and mineral matter that cover the surface of the earth.">soil resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1189" title="Field method used by earth scientists to study the underground structure of an area. A long narrow ditch is dug to locate geologic features, such as a fault.">trenching</a><br/>
